From 4e3a6ab837c6e9eacce922f2f417c0a394bb6f5d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 12:26:24 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] host_loop_lease: refresh a hand-off waiter's .want
 on its own timer

PR #2161 review nit 1 (review t_01a1d4bc67257c47, GitHub review 5890499145).

While a higher-priority standby waits on LOCK_EX for a hand-off, its .want
was refreshed only from held() once _next_probe passed. The refresh cadence
therefore depended on the caller's loop: a caller that calls held() less
than once per interval let its own .want pass the 3 x interval expiry in
_live_want, and the holder/standbys stopped deferring to it (it still got
the lock on release, but lost hand-off priority).

Fix: _want() starts a second daemon thread for the wait,
_refresh_want_while_waiting, which calls _keep_want() once per interval
under _mu for as long as that wait lasts (stops when the wait thread wins or
fails, on release(), or when the fd changed; reset after fork). held() keeps
its refresh as the fallback when the refresher thread cannot start (logged
as a WARNING; the wait itself continues). Module docstring updated.

Tests (tests/hermes_cli/test_host_loop_lease.py):
- test_waiter_keeps_its_want_live_without_held_calls: holder SIGSTOPped,
  waiter calls held() once, then waits (no held()) for a refresh made past the first record's 3 x interval expiry;
  a lower-priority lease object's _live_want() still returns the waiter's record.
  RED on origin/main (record expired, "ignoring stale test-loop.want"),
  GREEN with this change.
- test_refresher_spawn_failure_keeps_waiting_and_held_refreshes: only the
  refresher fails to start; the waiter stays waiting, held() refreshes .want
  and the waiter gets the lock on release.

Ran: test_host_loop_lease.py 24 passed (3 runs), tests/hermes_cli/test_doctor*.py
214 passed / 8 skipped, scripts/check --base origin/main.
